<topic id="GUID-FF3E08E4-B95F-4C08-8528-C23005B157A4" xml:lang="en-US"> 
  <title>Structural Testing - Static Compressive Load</title> 
  <body> 
	 <ul id="UL_5F1F2A3ED62240C1AE96323CE64C8EF4"> 
		<li id="LI_C7D4AAFBECCF4D4F878443E393A93F3A">Considerations should be made to ensure steady state static loading on the packages that does not exceed the limits recommended. Excessive steady state static loading can induce solder ball cracks, especially over a period of time resulting in higher failure rate. 
		</li> 
		<li id="LI_AB6205D8492446D4873A9CBB5214DC44">This static compressive load is not to be exceeded; therefore, the tolerance of the package and the tolerances of the thermal solution (including attach mechanism) should be considered when calculating or measuring static load on the package. 
		</li> 
		<li id="LI_468ED0C5E6854AF2997F1FD5A9F439CB">An ideal thermal solution design would apply a load as uniform as possible on all dies to optimize thermal performance and minimize mechanical risk. 
		</li> 
		<li id="LI_4DC51ED4F9F04435B08DD3F90825F23C"> Refer to Manufacturing with the Intel® Mobile Platform Code Named Wildcat Lake (#<xref href="https://cdrdv2.intel.com/v1/dl/getContent/861039" format="https" scope="external">861039</xref>) Manufacturing with WCL mobile processors for guidance on Corner Glue. 
		</li> 
	 </ul> 
